From 3cecb5ee86fbd696120231f5b701657e7b769180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:53:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Decode dense matmul: split-k GEMV with a completion-counter
 reduction (exl3_dgemv)

exl3_gemm now tries exl3_dgemv first for decode-shaped calls (m <= 16, k and n
multiples of 128, input/output transforms present). One regular launch, no grid
barrier: block (128-column group, k split) issues its weight prefetch, rotates
its k range of the input rows into shared memory (had_hf_r_128_inner, the
cooperative GEMM's input transform), runs the coop MoE GEMV tile over it with
fp32-accumulating MMAs (exl3_gemm's accumulation on sm_80+ other than sm_86)
and writes fp32 partials; the last of a group's arrivals sums them in split
order and applies the output transform (had_ff/fh_r_128_inner * svh). The
split-k factor comes from a waves x (k chunks + fixed cost) model over the
kernel's occupancy at its shared-memory size. Kernel arguments 0..9 are
exl3_gemm_kernel's, so graph recording is unchanged; the workspace (counters,
partials) is per device and allocated once.

It replaces the cooperative GEMM's fixed cost (grid barrier plus the serial
split-k chain through the column locks, ~15-20 us), so it takes the small
matrices: weight bytes up to 8 MB at m <= 8 and 2 MB at 9..16 rows
(EXL3_DGEMV_MAX_KB / _KB16; EXL3_DGEMV=0 off, 2 everywhere). gemv_tile gains
16-row MMAs, an aliased reduction area and fp32 accumulation as template
options; the MoE coop kernels are unchanged (bit-identical outputs).

GB10, MiniMax-M3.1 TP2-rank decode shapes, cold L2, default dispatch, A/B in
alternating processes (old -> new):
  k/v_proj 6144x256 K5:     4 rows 21.4-21.9 -> 10.9-11.6 us, 16 rows 25.6-26.0 -> 14.5 us
  shared gate/up 6144x1536 K4: 4 rows 30.2-30.3 -> 24.7-25.6 us (was the QTIP GEMV)
  shared down 1536x6144 K5: 4 rows 34.9-35.4 -> 31.2-31.4 us
  per verify step at the live call counts: c=1 17.0 -> 14.9 ms, c=4 18.1 -> 16.4 ms
Accuracy: rel error vs an fp32 reference 2.0-2.2e-4, same as the cooperative
GEMM (output difference ~5e-7 rel); 2.1e-4 vs 3.9e-4 where the fp16-accumulating
QTIP GEMV ran. Live-pack weights (layers 1 and 10, both TP2 ranks, rows 1..16)
pass test_qgemm's assert_close against reconstruct + fp16 matmul; test_moe_coop
passes.
